{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he said, Look, it is still, etc.</b> The reason he took it upon himself to judge them is on account of the pain of living creatures, which is a matter of Torah law (Bava Metzia 32b), and he was concerned for the flock. Furthermore, he wished to know whether the reason for their delay was that there was no time to water the flock and graze it, since the city was distant and the flocks were at home — and this matter was relevant for him to know the way of the world that had come to him, and from their answer he understood that it was not because of the city's distance that they were doing so."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:25.874705764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}